---
source: crates/leptoskit_db_macros/src/tests.rs
expression: "report.join(\"\\n\")"
---
no query: a view needs its query: `sql = "SELECT …"`, or `sql(postgres = "…", sqlite = "…")`
table option: unknown view option; expected `name`, `sql`, `materialized`, `namespace`, `public`, `projection`, `index`, `unique`, or `crate`
index on a plain view: only a materialized view keeps rows to index: add `materialized`, or drop `index(...)` and `unique(...)`
audit: unknown view option; expected `name`, `sql`, `materialized`, `namespace`, `public`, `projection`, `index`, `unique`, or `crate`
live: unknown view option; expected `name`, `sql`, `materialized`, `namespace`, `public`, `projection`, `index`, `unique`, or `crate`
one dialect: `sql(...)` needs both `postgres = "…"` and `sqlite = "…"`; for one expression on both, write `sql = "…"`
column option: a view's columns are what its query returns, so they take only `column`, `private`, `secret`, and `in(...)`
key: a view's columns are what its query returns, so they take only `column`, `private`, `secret`, and `in(...)`
write policy: a view is only read, so its policies govern `select`
sql on a table: `sql` and `materialized` describe a view: use `#[db::view(...)]`
